## Co-culture rescue of swarming by ΔrhlI + ΔlasI mixes
<!-- rho:session c-1bc17a12d9a43fba -->

### Question

Do ΔrhlI and ΔlasI, which each swarm poorly alone, swarm like wild type again when
grown together, and does the rescue depend on the ratio they are mixed at? Where is
the peak ratio, and how strong is the ratio effect?

### Data & method

- [data/swarming/cocultures.csv](data/swarming/cocultures.csv) — 45 dishes: wild type, ΔlasI and ΔrhlI grown alone, plus ΔrhlI:ΔlasI mixes at twelve ratios from 1:3 to 1000:1, three dishes per condition; `ratio_rhlI_to_lasI` reads ΔrhlI first, so 10:1 is ten ΔrhlI cells per ΔlasI cell. Records colony `area`, `circularity` and `roundness`.
- [analysis/swarming_cocultures.R](analysis/swarming_cocultures.R) — planned: log-scale colony area against mix ratio; a quadratic fit in log2 ratio to locate the peak with a bootstrap CI; Welch comparisons of mixes against wild type and each single mutant; ratio effect size; figure and table.

